## Original Content
El Consejo de Ministros celebra su primera reunión tras el parón veraniego.

## Summary
The Spanish government has approved a unified command in Ceuta to manage the return and repatriation of immigrants following a mass influx. The Council of Ministers made this decision in its first meeting after the summer break. This measure is aimed at handling the situation after a massive assault by immigrants.

## Key Points
- The government approved a unified command in Ceuta for immigrant management.
- The command is specifically for the return and repatriation of immigrants.
- The decision comes in response to a mass assault or influx of immigrants.
- The Council of Ministers convened for the first time after the summer break to address this issue.


